Am trying to get some linux systems approved for classified use within 
DOE.  I recently found your site and hope it will help in the effort.  I 
hope there are plans to continue the Open Source development of secure 
Linux in spite of Microsoft's objections.  We in the DOE community 
appreciate your efforts and hope they will continue and expand so as to 
give the government a secure alternative to Microsoft products.  I 
believe that Open Source development will be far better than closed 
source and save the government and taxpayer, of which I am one, money, 
time between new releases and have far fewer vulnerabilities.

Regards

Douglas Phillipson  (Bechtel Nevada, DOE Subcontractor)
